{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set","id":56155,"title":"Need Help Conceptualizing the Followers of Set","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T08:32:58-08:00","id":56155,"title":"Need Help Conceptualizing the Followers of Set","content":"I've got no idea what to do with these guys!<br /> <br /> They're named after an Egyptian god, but they worship their own weird force of darkness and destruction. This somehow gives them snake powers because of a vague connection to this Egyptian god (despite Set having nothing to do with snakes), and then they have a sort of vague tie to corruption and temptation via drug peddling. It just feels like this grab bag of thematic elements that don't mesh well at all.<br /> <br /> I'm almost tempted to look towards the Baali for covering the same ground in a much cleaner way. You have the religious zeal, you have the temptation and corruption, and you have a Discipline that makes a fair amount more sense.<br /> <br /> Can you help me out here? I don't want to have to ignore one of the core clans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:43:50-08:00","id":56162,"title":"","content":"Set was a servant/worshipper of Apep, a 'snake themed' being, who Set later kills and absorbs power from. Going by what happened in the diablerie of Tzimisce and Saulot, it is also quite possible that Apep defeated Set and assumed his identity instead.<br /> <br /> All of these account (to some extent) for the 'snake theme'. That said, for a Clan of corruptors, the Sense the Sin power from Daimonion would be a much better fit.<br /> <br /> A very good YouTube vid on the Settites, by The Gentleman Gamer:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q-XZdEgbCIo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q-XZdEgbCIo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q-XZdEgbCIo\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q-XZdEgbCIo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if a Chronicle needs both Settites and Baali, I prefer the former they don't require the inclusion of demons into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","user":"harlokin","date":". 01-23-2014, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:40:32-08:00","id":56194,"title":"","content":"While I entirely agree that in many respects Baali and Setites have very similar thematics and ideas, and the themes of the Setites can be somewhat confused in many of the books because there was either not enough room for detail or not all of the writers quite understood what they were writing. In my experience I've found the following:<br /> <br /> Baali work much better as an antagnoist in a chronicle, especially with their massive infernalist influences and overtones, their actions and schemes can range from the small term mayhem to the grandoise infernal design. Even the most dispirate of characters will be able to work together to fight off the Baali, they are the similar but slightly 'outside' antagnoist that all the factions can hate, especially in a Dark Ages chronicle. Consider that the primary clans that continue to work against the Baali are Assamites, Salubri and Setites.<br /> <br /> Setites on the other hand I've found work much better when written as potential allies, because they exist outside of the political structures of the western courts they have every reason to offer their services to various factions in exchange for protection. This means that they have to prove themselves exceedingly useful to be kept around despite their strange ways and unseemly reputation. I've found then that Setites work best when used as the competition for clans such as the Nosferatu and Tremere, in part because of their own networks of informants and their own mystical capabilities which are usually outside that understood by western cainites. You can even have the Setites at first demand much smaller boons in recompense, lull the characters in believing that they've resisted their attempts at corruption and manipulation by making them obvious and playing to the sterotypes, all the while the Setites are actually playing a much more subtle game of corruption. They have centuries to wait afterall, and they'd rather have more allies and eventual converts than blow it on something crass. The drugs, prostiution and other inequity is just the very basic stuff that the Setites can be doing, they can also be providing information, criminal services outside the hands of the usual elders of the city, mystical assistance, social assistance, anything you can think of.<br /> The Setites then become strong allies of the down on their luck or unconnected characters, reguardless of what tier the players exist on they can provide an edge that their enemies do not neccesarily have. All the while they are being led very slowly through the revelations, so slowly that the characters will never notice it until its too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:55:19-08:00","id":56266,"title":"","content":"A few things to mention<br /> <br /> Major thing: The FoS all have a connecting Ethos. Namely, the FoS believe the gods and similar beings constrain people and vampires, keeping them as their slaves for worship. The FoS have kind of a faux-Gnostic approach of believing they need to break down the societal web which constrains the true essence of beings; the idea that some god can tell you what you can and can't do. And many see the many rules of society as a similar web of shoulds cast over mankind and Vampirekind. At their best, the Setites wish to liberate others from this slavery and web. It's how the Aeons or gods stay on top and keep humans weak and vampires under control.<br /> <br /> But they can't be mistaken for good guys any more than other Vampires can. They tend to do it by breaking people, bringing them to rock bottom and rebuilding them in their image. The debasement, in theory, is to aggressively force a reexamination of worldview. This also tends to put people in their debt. But many never reach that point. These talents for debasement often let a Setite pursue their goals by controlling other Cainites and trying to break down the Camarilla or Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Setites also tend to control many ancient sites, and have access to troves of ancient lore. They are in many ways guardians of secrets of the past, and in that vein they learned to negotiate with Cainites who want what they have.<br /> <br /> The Baali lack a coherant ethos. Some are demon worshipers, others follow &quot;the hive&quot; while still others seek to facilitate the return of the Children...or prevent it. Some Baali actively strive to keep the Children asleep and prevent the end of the world. Those who are demon worshipers are pretty easy, pop culture gives us a thousand uses for them. The Hive followers are strange, and make for a more truly alien encounter then any Setite or the other sorts of Baali. And those seeking to hasten the destruction of the world via the Children are also truly mad, often trying to unearth one's resting place.<br /> <br /> This means the Baali and Setites want some different things. Infernal Baali want souls for their master. Setites tend to be disinterested in souls. Either the PCs are pawns or the PCs are worthy of being freed from the Aeons, one or the other. Baali on either side of the conflict with the Children or those of the hive tend to be less interested in corrupting PCs, though the hive ones may want to add to the swarm. This is not to say a Baali trying to awaken one of the children or a Baali trying to keep them asleep have no use for the PCs, but it is less driving. While somewhat similar, the two lines have clear differences.<br /> <br /> In modern day especially, too, the FoS vastly outnumber the Baali. The Baali are a Bloodline, and one in decline, so their numbers are a fraction of the FoS...you could probably fit them all in one apartment. The Followers of Set would fill a complex, possibly more. This is slightly less of a spread in a Victorian Age game though there is still a large outnumbering, and in Dark Ages their numbers may be close, with Setites only having slightly more.<br /> <br /> Their magic, again not a direct theme, is pretty different. The Setites practice Akhu, an Egyption sorta Necromantic magic, while the Baali if anything tend to practice Dark Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Does this help?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T10:53:49-07:00","id":729352,"title":"","content":"Joined just to post on this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You're absolutely right on the Baali, as they are a much more straightforward group. They're evil demon worshippers interested in souls, demonology and generally bad things. As tempters for the sake of corruption, as eviler-than-thou antagonists and as Demon-themed monsters they do much better than Setites. It's true what the Baroness says about their motives being rather heterogeneous, but simply put, they're much more straightforward.<br /> <br /> The Setites, indeed, are a rather confused bunch in-canon. Clearly, the writers themselves didn't know exactly where to go with them, or had vastly different opinions on it, and as a result the Setites' background, motives and role are much more vague. That's not at all a bad thing, as you can basically do with them whatever you want. They're an open invitation to be creative with a clan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As such, they have a few narrative advantages:<br /> <br /> 1) Mystery:Remember that you, or at least the players, don't <i>have </i>to know everything either. The Setites have one thematic going for them vis-\u00e0-vis the Baali, and that's their emphasis on <i>knowledge, manipulation of history and secrecy.</i> All the irritating Egyptian clich\u00e9s might in the end just be an efficient act just to cover what's going on underneath. The only thing you're bound to keep as a certainty is the snake-fixation, as their discipline is based on that.<br /> <br /> 2) AncientKnowledge<i>: </i>Sure, the Baali also dwell in ancient lore, as so many clans do, but the Setites are <i>old. </i>One text mentions them being much older than Caine. I really liked that thought, but little has been done with it afterwards. The Setites and their master are easily linked with ancient astronaut- and chariot of the gods- theories, and even with Cthulhu-type stories if that's your thing. If you want an explanation for Serpentis, read David Icke's mad (but real!) theories on reptilian monsters with strange powers visiting earth for millennia before humanity, from other dimensions, and <i>their offspring posing as humans</i>. This might look far fetched, even for a vampire game, but the longer you think about it, the better it fits. Take for example the location: Setites are canonically 'big' in Egypt, India, and originally in Latin America... three regions abundantly mentioned in alien conspiracy theories, with pyramids and other impressive structures claimed to be constructed with unknown technology and with serpent like creatures appearing as gods.<br /> <br /> 3) The Necessary Evil: Setites are considered Evil in most cases, but they're not so bad that they basically have a killed-on-sight guarantee. You mentioned replacing them with Baali, but a known organization consisting of these straightforward monsters would be much more difficult to explain, as no neighboring kindred organization would allow it to exist at all. In fact, a lot of canon tells about how Kindred groups unite against all odds every single time a Baali organization rises to the surface, and I believe this to be belief worthy. The Baali cannot be reasoned with, and the only proper way to deal with them is utter destruction. They're true fanatics, as you said. The Setites might have motives that are as bad, but at least on the surface they're willing to deal with others. Whatever they're hiding, openly they look more like ultra-orthodox believers in some weird ancient religion than in extremists trying to bring as much evil in the world as possible.<br /> <br /> The previous posts are very old already, so I don't know if it's appreciated that I still answer this, but this is a theme that one can find very little on, while it's actually a good question, so I took the shot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Knuddel!<br /> <br /> G","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8895-grossstadt","name":"Grossstadt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T21:34:04-07:00","id":731216,"title":"","content":"I personally greatly prefer the Baali over the Setites, because the latter are poorly written at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T02:26:41-07:00","id":731788,"title":"","content":"Others have answered the questions so I won't repeat them, but it's funny you should ask this as I got around to reading Clanbook: Followers of Set Revised just the other night. Prior to doing so I had the same impression of the Setites and not only do I have a new appreciation for the depth of the clan but I fully intend to play a Setite character at some point. I strongly recommend picking up the book if you're interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T03:55:51-07:00","id":731863,"title":"","content":"The Baali are a sledgehammer. The Followers of Set are a scalpel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:48:53-07:00","id":732841,"title":"","content":"Also you can have friendly Followers of Seth (Hell the protagonist of their Dark Ages Novel is one of the most moral characters in the series). Friendly Baali? Not so much. The fact that for all their faults the Setites aren't in the buisness of summoning/enslaving/controlling Eldritch Abominations is a big factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:25:40-07:00","id":733461,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in any of the books about Baali not being friendly. Hell, there's only ONE major book on them: Clanbook Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T20:45:15-07:00","id":733809,"title":"","content":"I think the Setites need to be broadened. 4th Edition is a good opportunity. Make them worshippers of a more vague snake being. Be it the the Biblical Serpent, Set/Apep, Jormungandr, Quetzalcoatl, or even Tiamat. They should also probably take on the &quot;vice&quot; aspect from the Ravnos (and leave the Ravnos, or their replacement, with the &quot;nomad&quot; aspect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T03:35:33-07:00","id":734186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=733809#post733809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Setites need to be broadened. 4th Edition is a good opportunity. Make them worshippers of a more vague snake being. Be it the the Biblical Serpent, Set/Apep, Jormungandr, Quetzalcoatl, or even Tiamat. They should also probably take on the &quot;vice&quot; aspect from the Ravnos (and leave the Ravnos, or their replacement, with the &quot;nomad&quot; aspect).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revised edition clanbook makes references to a few of these. It talks about &quot;old tales and new rumours&quot; of a bloodline in the Americas called the Tlacique who have the discipline of Protean instead of Serpentis, it also talks about how Arnulf Jormungangrsson attempted to build a cult around the Midgard serpent and was Primogen of Christiana/Oslo for a time. There are numerous other examples, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T14:57:13-08:00","id":1549026,"title":"","content":"DREAD THREAD NECROMANCY STRIKES AGAIN! I made an account just so I could give my two pence on this. <br /> <br /> I love everything about the Setites (down to the snake motif) <i>except for</i> the whole Egyptian shtick. Not only was it poorly implemented, but for a game whose primary mythos is based on Abrahamic religions, it sticks out awkwardly like a sore thumb. On the other hand, I love the Satanic aesthetics of the Baali but I don't care for their &quot;let's end the world&quot; nihilism nor their &quot;let's kill babies to prevent the end of the world.&quot; So, what I do is combine them into a single clan, which I name The Serpents of Eden. They keep their snake theming, their gnostic philosophy, their utilizing sin to guide others to enlightenment, the whole &quot;breaking the chains of God,&quot; but tie the main mythos to Satan/Lucifer and the Fall of Man. They definitely have splinter groups like (you guessed it) Egyptian Serpents who view Satan through the mask of Set, Nordic Serpents who worship Loki, and then the bastard children (the Baali) who don't want enlightenment but want destruction. In the modern nights, they are also commonly associated with The Fallen, seeing them as infernal divinity in human flesh (which is somewhat true).<br /> <br /> All of that said, I think V5 did a very nice job reconceptualizing the Setites into the Ministry, making it a lot more free-form and less dependent on Egyptian mythos, basically doing what I mentioned above but without forcing ties to any one mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28754-doctorfaustus","name":"DoctorFaustus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T15:15:07-08:00","id":1549029,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I rather like the way that the Setites offer a vaguely-plausible alternative to the \u2018Curse of Cain\u2019 theory of vampirism (Whether their own \u2018Just So\u2019 story is right or wrong).<br /> <br /> Still, if you\u2019re looking for alternate takes on the Setites, you could do worse than to consider their <i>antitribu</i> the \u2018Serpents of Light\u2019 (A name which seems to scan with your own notions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T17:34:17-08:00","id":1549035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoctorFaustus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549026#post1549026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DREAD THREAD NECROMANCY STRIKES AGAIN! I made an account just so I could give my two pence on this.<br /> <br /> I love everything about the Setites (down to the snake motif) <i>except for</i> the whole Egyptian shtick. Not only was it poorly implemented, but for a game whose primary mythos is based on Abrahamic religions, it sticks out awkwardly like a sore thumb. On the other hand, I love the Satanic aesthetics of the Baali but I don't care for their &quot;let's end the world&quot; nihilism nor their &quot;let's kill babies to prevent the end of the world.&quot; So, what I do is combine them into a single clan, which I name The Serpents of Eden. They keep their snake theming, their gnostic philosophy, their utilizing sin to guide others to enlightenment, the whole &quot;breaking the chains of God,&quot; but tie the main mythos to Satan/Lucifer and the Fall of Man. They definitely have splinter groups like (you guessed it) Egyptian Serpents who view Satan through the mask of Set, Nordic Serpents who worship Loki, and then the bastard children (the Baali) who don't want enlightenment but want destruction. In the modern nights, they are also commonly associated with The Fallen, seeing them as infernal divinity in human flesh (which is somewhat true).<br /> <br /> All of that said, I think V5 did a very nice job reconceptualizing the Setites into the Ministry, making it a lot more free-form and less dependent on Egyptian mythos, basically doing what I mentioned above but without forcing ties to any one mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like the idea that you have there Doctor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T20:59:43-08:00","id":1549041,"title":"","content":"I also appreciate the idea that Set when he defeated Apep and gained some of that monster personality/essence and setting the seeds of a gradual personality change or the battle was so intense that a new composite being was &quot;born&quot; that has elements of both Set and Apep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T01:59:08-08:00","id":1549044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoctorFaustus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549026#post1549026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DREAD THREAD NECROMANCY STRIKES AGAIN! I made an account just so I could give my two pence on this.<br /> <br /> I love everything about the Setites (down to the snake motif) <i>except for</i> the whole Egyptian shtick. Not only was it poorly implemented, but for a game whose primary mythos is based on Abrahamic religions, it sticks out awkwardly like a sore thumb. On the other hand, I love the Satanic aesthetics of the Baali but I don't care for their &quot;let's end the world&quot; nihilism nor their &quot;let's kill babies to prevent the end of the world.&quot; So, what I do is combine them into a single clan, which I name The Serpents of Eden. They keep their snake theming, their gnostic philosophy, their utilizing sin to guide others to enlightenment, the whole &quot;breaking the chains of God,&quot; but tie the main mythos to Satan/Lucifer and the Fall of Man. They definitely have splinter groups like (you guessed it) Egyptian Serpents who view Satan through the mask of Set, Nordic Serpents who worship Loki, and then the bastard children (the Baali) who don't want enlightenment but want destruction. In the modern nights, they are also commonly associated with The Fallen, seeing them as infernal divinity in human flesh (which is somewhat true).<br /> <br /> All of that said, I think V5 did a very nice job reconceptualizing the Setites into the Ministry, making it a lot more free-form and less dependent on Egyptian mythos, basically doing what I mentioned above but without forcing ties to any one mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to add that I like this take on the Setites. I like the tying them to the Abrahamic meta mythology of the VtM mythos, ditching the Baali (or rolling them into the Setites, as long as the Baali are gone I'm fine) and divorcing them from a specific human culture in their main cultural influence.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that while I can see the point of letting the Setites stick out from the Abrahamic meta mythology of VtM, it always felt more odd than interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T14:28:14-08:00","id":1549054,"title":"","content":"I will mention that medieval Europe had almost no conception of what ancient Egypt was like, to the point that even in the early Renaissance, artists were still portraying Bible stories from Exodus with Pharaoh and Moses looking like contemporary Europeans. So, most Setites in Dark Ages Europe, outside of a few elder-run cults, are most likely to view their clan and its anti-Aeonic philosophies through the lens of the Serpent in the Garden from Genesis. This may even result in some who follow the Road of Heaven and see themselves akin to the Devil Tigers, tasked by God with testing the virtuous and destroying the weak of faith. Probably also some interesting takes on the Roads of Sin and Humanity as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T15:53:50-08:00","id":1549057,"title":"","content":"We all fall prey to cultural biasis at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T17:53:43-08:00","id":1549065,"title":"","content":"Especially when hieroglyphs fall victim to the Curse of Babel after quite a long period of disuse and the collapse of the scribal schools that helped maintain their use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T10:29:00-08:00","id":1549085,"title":"","content":"I like what was done with the Setites in VDA20, with three bloodlines (Followers of Set - the Priests -, Warriors of Glycon - the rulers, merchants and warriors -, and the Witches of Echidna - the mystics). The clan was more Meidterranean mythology oriented, with Typhon and Echidna as the Father and Mother, though local myths and theologies were welcome. There was a lot more emphasis on snakes and the Egyptian fanatics of Set were not yet the dominant force of the clan, which was therefore much more than just &quot;Egyptian&quot;. Between the core manula, Tome of Secrets and the Companion there are many intriguing ideas to imagine what the real origin of the clan was and what was its shape and form in ancient times. The transformation of the clan into an Egyptian cult of Set is explained by the fact that the Priest bloodline gets rid of the other two, takes leadership of the clan from the Warriors of Glycon, takes magic from the Witches of Echidna, and creates its own pseudo-bloodline of bodyguards trained in Potence to replace the muscle of the Warriors of Glycon with brawn more loyal to the Priests. <br /> <br /> If one likes the snake theme, it's worth perusing that material to come up with a true snake clan which was gradually overrun by its Egyptian faction worshipping the aardvark-headed, Apep-slaughtering Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T10:31:38-08:00","id":1549086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549054#post1549054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will mention that medieval Europe had almost no conception of what ancient Egypt was like, to the point that even in the early Renaissance, artists were still portraying Bible stories from Exodus with Pharaoh and Moses looking like contemporary Europeans. So, most Setites in Dark Ages Europe, outside of a few elder-run cults, are most likely to view their clan and its anti-Aeonic philosophies through the lens of the Serpent in the Garden from Genesis. This may even result in some who follow the Road of Heaven and see themselves akin to the Devil Tigers, tasked by God with testing the virtuous and destroying the weak of faith. Probably also some interesting takes on the Roads of Sin and Humanity as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coupled with the snake stuff I mentioned in my previous comment, one could argue that European Setites in the Dark Ages were more familiar with the Serpent in the Garden than with Set because that was actually more like the local Setite tradition along with pagan snake stuff. One could suggest that pagan snake stuff was there first, and then Middle Eastern Bible-influenced Setites migrated Westward with the spread of Christianity. Egyptian stuff came in only much later, when the Egyptian Priests got rid of the other bloodlines and did a make over to the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 03-08-2025, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T14:34:31-08:00","id":1549092,"title":"","content":"Something that a thread like this gives me a chance to think about is that Egypt in general has a lot of interesting possibilities for the history of WoD/VtM that I\u2019d be curious to hear others opinions about.<br /> <br /> I recently read \u2018The Mediterranean in the Ancient World\u2019 by Fernand Braudel and one of the things I took away from it were how his historical insights into the ancient near East could be useful for WoD/VtM lore. Braudel argues that throughout the height of the Mediterranean Bronze Age (which he places c. 2500-1200 BCE) the two central nodes of civilization and trade and the region came from Mesopotamia &amp; Egypt.<br /> <br /> Mesopotamia is almost tailor made for vampires and the Jyhad. A large number of unique and independent city-states, constantly competing amongst each other for advantage, each boasting their own tutelary gods and claims to fame, while still being loosely interconnected by common ties of religion and language. It\u2019s so easy for me to imagine how each of the clans (or at least most of them) could divide the cities up between there 4th &amp; 5th Gen members in the Bronze Age and compete against one another. Even during periods of relative hegemony, such as under the Akkadian or Babylonian Empires, the individual cities still retained a lot of localized power. I can readily imagine that whatever clans represent the cities of Babylon or Ur (Ventrue or Toreador would probably be a good fit) could produce a number of early traditions to allow for relatively safe contact and commerce between the vampiric courts while still each city remained relatively independent of one another.<br /> <br /> Egypt, on the other hand, seems to be different. After the early unification of the upper &amp; lower kingdoms and the reunification into the Middle Kingdom after the First Intermediary Period, Egypt seems to have been relatively stably organized around the central power of the pharaoh\u2019s court, with local courts only gaining relatively greater autonomy during intermediary periods. This isn\u2019t really surprising if one takes a look at geography of course. While Mesopotamia has a vast flood plain for its relatively autonomous city-states to spread across, the vast majority of Egyptian civilization is united by the Nile: whoever controls the levers of central authority, at any time other than those of utter collapse, can maintain hegemony across almost all of Egypt with relative ease. <br /> <br /> What this would seem to imply to me is that, until the period of Egypt\u2019s conquest by outside powers, the vampiric leadership of Egypt ought to have been relatively homogenous. Perhaps in Bronze Age Egypt we would even see proto-types of the high-low clan distinction with different clans having designated roles in the social hierarchy of Egypt.<br /> <br /> (Checking the wiki it seems to suggest that the Settites did predominate in Egypt until the conquests of the Hellenic &amp; Roman empires which id agree with, although perhaps I\u2019d even suggest the Assyrian or Persian empires of the early Iron Age as the point of divergence)<br /> <br /> I imagine much of the strange and sometimes contradictory lore regarding Set/Sutekh/Horus/Osiris/Isis/etc. as having occurred sometime before the period of recorded Egyptian history proper, at the unification of the Upper &amp; Lower Kingdoms at the latest, but probably occurring in pre-dynastic Egypt in general, sometime between the era of the Second City &amp; the rise of the Old Kingdom.<br /> <br /> This leaves us at least 2,000 years where the Settites may predominate in Egypt. The scope of that period is vast of course but developing ideas about what it was like could be helpful for ideas about the Settites in general. My mind is drawn towards the ancient vampire king &amp; queen of Egypt from the Vampire Chronicles books (The Vampire Lestat &amp; Queen of the Damned) in particular. The portrayal of those characters, who probably influenced the very concept of Methuselahs in general, seem like an interesting way that Egypt could be handled. A central god-like object of cult devotion, perhaps Set himself in the beginning or members of the 4th generation, with the rest of the clan emerging outward in expanding spheres to serve the god and maintain their holy domain in the Egyptian nights.<br /> <br /> In this context, with the mysterious destruction of Set around the turn of the millennium and the waves of conquests washing over Egypt from the Assyrians to the Arabs, I think one gets an interesting image that preserves the early Settites vibe of being a defeated and scattered priesthood of a dead god, hailing back to a Hyperborean age which to the moderns may feel more akin to Atlantis or Lemuria than their own relatively recent and mundane histories, and gives the feeling of a central hook to the clan\u2019s narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T11:08:55-07:00","id":1549244,"title":"","content":"I may be the odd one out here, but to me, the &quot;serpent&quot; element is the least interesting part of the Setites, so doubling down on that seems the wrong way to go. Moreover, making the game even more Abrahamic (and really, mostly Christian) is just so obvious and has been done to death.<br /> <br /> Now, a clan of worship and rebellion/faith and taboo, and the cults that surround them, feels like it has more scope. Drop the Followers of Set name (except maybe for those old Egyptian priests), and the even worse Ministry name, and keep Mesu Bedshet (Children of the Revolution). That's what they called themselves anyway.<br /> <br /> Instead of snake-themed powers, they could have powers based on their religious animal affinities \u2014 everything from ibises to crocodiles for Egyptian Mesu Bedshet, but with room for jaguars or herons for the South American Tlacique, roosters or bulls for the Caribbean Wangateurs, and freshwater turtles or cobras for the Children of Damballah. I also had new lineages that were Italian, Iberian, and Iraqi/Iranian.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this flexibility justifies Protean over Serpentis with some unique and cool combo powers, or else a broadened version of Serpentis with different paths. If it's Protean, they take the form of sacred animals instead of the traditional wolf or bat. In my games, I'd already renamed their Discipline Djiwas (= Given Dominion/Power, from the was-sceptre of Set), with the different paths called &quot;Serekhs&quot; (literally &quot;facade&quot;, but also a hieroglyph which symbolised the gate of a palace and indicated that the subject was royal). So the Serekh of Serpentis is the Greek-based Gnostic/Typhonic pathway, while the Serekh of Sha (=Typhonic beast) is the pathway of the traditional Set animal form.<br /> <br /> The focus of the Discipline would expand from just taking on animal features to adopting divine features which may include animal elements, so that you can essentially become a jackal-headed god or bird-headed garuda, etc. They can be biblical entities, if you would prefer that \u2014 think about how weird the angels are in the Old Testament, with four animal heads, etc, and you've got a good basis for the profane-divine forms of an Abrahamic Mesu Bedshet.<br /> <br /> In the original <i>Clanbook: Setite</i>, they also got in-clan access to the Path of Corruption, without needing to learn Thaumaturgy otherwise. That made a good alternative to Serpentis for many character concepts, so keeping the Priest/Warrior/Witch castes with the ability of the last to learn the Path of Corruption as part of Akhu is appealing.<br /> <br /> What I like best about this approach is that it doesn't invalidate what came before \u2014 snakey Setites are still a thing, but you also broaden the thematics of the clan without having to go as far as smooshing two different clans/bloodlines together. To me, this is just doubling down on the core elements that were already there and then adding extra options in for flexibility. Also, the divine/profane duality is really interesting to me, but doesn't force you to go down one particular route (either Gnostic or Ancient Egyptian).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-13-2025, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:22:03-07:00","id":1549265,"title":"","content":"I read in one of the books about the Nordics, (maybe it was for Ars Magica, but, that, there are Setties in the Viking-lands of Scandinavia. I can imagine them building a pyramid, which is so out of place there. Reminds be of playing Age of Mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:27:41-07:00","id":1549267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549029#post1549029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be honest, I rather like the way that the Setites offer a vaguely-plausible alternative to the \u2018Curse of Cain\u2019 theory of vampirism (Whether their own \u2018Just So\u2019 story is right or wrong).<br /> <br /> Still, if you\u2019re looking for alternate takes on the Setites, you could do worse than to consider their <i>antitribu</i> the \u2018Serpents of Light\u2019 (A name which seems to scan with your own notions).</div> </div> </div> </div>I too often disregard the, &quot;Curse of Cain&quot;, seeing how vampires have been around for thousands of years, and yet, the most popular-religion in their domains just happens to be their back-story. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:52:47-07:00","id":1549270,"title":"","content":"I do have a soft spot for the idea that Set is the father of vampires and even Dark Ages Ravnos had their own creation myth of how they came to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T00:56:02-07:00","id":1549288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549244#post1549244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be the odd one out here, but to me, the &quot;serpent&quot; element is the least interesting part of the Setites, so doubling down on that seems the wrong way to go. Moreover, making the game even more Abrahamic (and really, mostly Christian) is just so obvious and has been done to death.<br /> <br /> Now, a clan of worship and rebellion/faith and taboo, and the cults that surround them, feels like it has more scope. Drop the Followers of Set name (except maybe for those old Egyptian priests), and the even worse Ministry name, and keep Mesu Bedshet (Children of the Revolution). That's what they called themselves anyway.<br /> <br /> Instead of snake-themed powers, they could have powers based on their religious animal affinities \u2014 everything from ibises to crocodiles for Egyptian Mesu Bedshet, but with room for jaguars or herons for the South American Tlacique, roosters or bulls for the Caribbean Wangateurs, and freshwater turtles or cobras for the Children of Damballah. I also had new lineages that were Italian, Iberian, and Iraqi/Iranian.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this flexibility justifies Protean over Serpentis with some unique and cool combo powers, or else a broadened version of Serpentis with different paths. If it's Protean, they take the form of sacred animals instead of the traditional wolf or bat. In my games, I'd already renamed their Discipline Djiwas (= Given Dominion/Power, from the was-sceptre of Set), with the different paths called &quot;Serekhs&quot; (literally &quot;facade&quot;, but also a hieroglyph which symbolised the gate of a palace and indicated that the subject was royal). So the Serekh of Serpentis is the Greek-based Gnostic/Typhonic pathway, while the Serekh of Sha (=Typhonic beast) is the pathway of the traditional Set animal form.<br /> <br /> The focus of the Discipline would expand from just taking on animal features to adopting divine features which may include animal elements, so that you can essentially become a jackal-headed god or bird-headed garuda, etc. They can be biblical entities, if you would prefer that \u2014 think about how weird the angels are in the Old Testament, with four animal heads, etc, and you've got a good basis for the profane-divine forms of an Abrahamic Mesu Bedshet.<br /> <br /> In the original <i>Clanbook: Setite</i>, they also got in-clan access to the Path of Corruption, without needing to learn Thaumaturgy otherwise. That made a good alternative to Serpentis for many character concepts, so keeping the Priest/Warrior/Witch castes with the ability of the last to learn the Path of Corruption as part of Akhu is appealing.<br /> <br /> What I like best about this approach is that it doesn't invalidate what came before \u2014 snakey Setites are still a thing, but you also broaden the thematics of the clan without having to go as far as smooshing two different clans/bloodlines together. To me, this is just doubling down on the core elements that were already there and then adding extra options in for flexibility. Also, the divine/profane duality is really interesting to me, but doesn't force you to go down one particular route (either Gnostic or Ancient Egyptian).</div> </div> </div> </div>The focus on the snake theme in VDA20 could be used to do exactly what you're saying: the manuals in fact speak of East African (if memory serves me well) Setites, the Indian Daityas, the Norse children of Jormungandr, and later on there will be the children of Damballah and the Serpents of the Light. Basically, one can plug into snake myths from every culture and Setites' religiosity is quite varied in that framework. The East African ones for example are very politheist, nothing in the Tome of Secrets (where they get a few lines more than elsewhere) suggests they are even remotely in the same business as Egyptian Setites (i.e. pick one god from the pantheon and worship him against the rest). The manual does say that those Setites are those that advised the Egyptian ones to cut off the rest, but the reason why is up to speculation.<br /> <br /> The snake theme can also be used to suggest a connection to Lilith, since Serpent is one of her forms and she did have a fling with a demon, and demons feed on faith. But then we do fall back onto Christian imaginary with that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are multiple ways to go about this. I do find yours quite interesting, especially with the nice details like using the names Djiwas and Serekh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T01:02:52-07:00","id":1549289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549265#post1549265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read in one of the books about the Nordics, (maybe it was for Ars Magica, but, that, there are Setties in the Viking-lands of Scandinavia. I can imagine them building a pyramid, which is so out of place there. Reminds be of playing Age of Mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nordic Setites don't build pyramids, they exalt Jormungandr and Loki. Basically they're well integrated in Norse culture (even if in a negative role), like most Setite cults except the specific Egyptian branch which then overtook the main Western ones - including the one from Constantinople, actually based on the Garden of Eden story. A Western Christendom branch should have looked like the children of Judas, but instead those were eliminated and, while their ideas end influencing later Setism, the Victorian Age and Masquerade Setites take the egyptologist niche, which is rather reductive and makes them look out of place. There are some gnostic and greco-roman cults surviving though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T09:28:50-07:00","id":1549396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549267#post1549267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I too often disregard the, &quot;Curse of Cain&quot;, seeing how vampires have been around for thousands of years, and yet, the most popular-religion in their domains just happens to be their back-story.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty I\u2019m perfectly happy to run with the Curse of Cain myself, but I do like to see the setting at least offer examples of vampires trying to work out a alternative explanations - whether or not they are more objectively true.<br /> <br /> After all, I don\u2019t actually LIKE vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":"Replacement of \u2018holy\u2019 with \u2018happy\u2019). 03-18-2025, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T19:09:54-07:00","id":1549508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549289#post1549289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nordic Setites don't build pyramids, they exalt Jormungandr and Loki. Basically they're well integrated in Norse culture (even if in a negative role), like most Setite cults except the specific Egyptian branch which then overtook the main Western ones - including the one from Constantinople, actually based on the Garden of Eden story. A Western Christendom branch should have looked like the children of Judas, but instead those were eliminated and, while their ideas end influencing later Setism, the Victorian Age and Masquerade Setites take the egyptologist niche, which is rather reductive and makes them look out of place. There are some gnostic and greco-roman cults surviving though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Settie Antitribu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T21:50:34-07:00","id":1549515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/56155-need-help-conceptualizing-the-followers-of-set?p=1549508#post1549508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original Settie Antitribu?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please clarify? Because I mentioned several groups, but none of them have been described in the lore as original Setite antitribu, and of course the latter are usually the Sabbat Serpents of the Light and their ancestors, the Children of Damballah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}